tmkc:GC-0081 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual calls use a concept fundamental to trade mark law and lists the questions it bears on: capability to distinguish, honest concurrent or prior use, ownership. Section 6 says its meaning is 'affected by' subsections 7(1), (2) and (3) — which is not the same as being defined by them."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "trade mark use"@en-AU,
        "use"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the concept's place in the scheme and the Act tells us where its meaning is affected. Held as one concept with the specialised uses — authorised, prior, honest concurrent — as separate records beside it, because each answers a different question under a different provision."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'use in the course of trade' should be the preferred label. Section 17 makes the course of trade part of what a trade mark is, and the bare word 'use' may be too wide for a vocabulary that also holds authorised use and prior use."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0081" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s7> ;
    tmk:notLabel "authorised use"@en-AU,
        "evidence of use"@en-AU,
        "honest concurrent use"@en-AU,
        "prior use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0081 .

tmkc:GC-0082 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Control by the owner is the whole of it: section 8(2) makes use authorised only to the extent the user acts under the owner's control. Section 7(3) then treats authorised use as use by the owner, which is why it matters to section 41 and section 44(4)."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "authorised use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "authorised use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 8 defines it and limits it by control. Held apart from 'authorised user' because the Act defines the person in 8(1) and the use in 8(2), and evidence questions attach to the second."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be a Part 19A passage on control rather than the general opening. This record cites the opening because it names authorised use in the list of questions use bears on."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0082" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s7(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8(2)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "assignment"@en-AU,
        "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0082 .

tmkc:GC-0083 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The person, as against the use. Section 8(1) makes control the test for both, but the Act keeps them in separate subsections and section 26 gives the authorised user rights of its own."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "authorised user"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms by section 8(1). Note the repository already holds GC-0035 for this term from the section 43 pilot; this record is written from the statutory definition rather than from Part 29's use of the phrase, and the two should be reconciled by a reviewer rather than by an agent."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The overlap with the signed GC-0035. If they are the same concept this record should be retired in favour of the signed one; if the section 43 sense is narrower, both stand and need a relationship between them."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0083" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/authorised-user>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8(1)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "authorised use"@en-AU,
        "predecessor in title"@en-AU,
        "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0083 .

tmkc:GC-0084 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Defined by the Register: the person in whose name the mark is registered. That is narrower than ownership at common law, and the Manual's Part 19B treats the registration as personal property held by that person."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "owner of the trade mark"@en-AU,
        "registered proprietor"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
