tmkc:GC-0090 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 44 turns on a comparison of priority dates, and a convention claim can move one. Distinct from the filing date, which section 6 defines separately, though for many applications the two coincide. GC-0016 already holds this term from the section 43 pilot."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "priority date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined by section 12 and pointed to by section 6. Written from the statute rather than from Part 29, which is what GC-0016 rests on; the overlap is flagged rather than resolved."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part11/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The overlap with the signed GC-0016. One of the two should be retired by a reviewer, and an agent may not choose which."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0090" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s12>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/priority-date> ;
    tmk:notLabel "date of registration"@en-AU,
        "filing date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s12>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/priority-date> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0090 .

tmkc:GC-0091 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 41(3)(b) makes use 'before the filing date' the thing that can rescue a mark with no inherent adaptation, so the filing date is not merely administrative."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "filing date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The section 6 definition is a stub continuing into a list, so the evidence is drawn from section 41(3)(b), where the date does operative work."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be a Part 10 or Part 11 passage that states how a filing date is set."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0091" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/filing-date> ;
    tmk:notLabel "date of registration"@en-AU,
        "priority date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0091 .

tmkc:GC-0092 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 31 gives examination two subjects and only two: whether the application was made in accordance with the Act, and whether there are grounds for rejecting it. Section 33 then makes acceptance the default unless the Registrar is satisfied of one of those."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "examine and report"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "examination"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 31 states the duty and its two subjects in one sentence. Held because the whole corpus is an examination manual and the vocabulary had no word for the activity it describes."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be a Part 5 or Part 6 passage about the examination process rather than Part 20.5 on grounds."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0092" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s31>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> ;
    tmk:notLabel "expedited examination"@en-AU,
        "hearing"@en-AU,
        "opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s31> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0092 .

tmkc:GC-0093 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 33(1) makes acceptance mandatory unless the Registrar is satisfied of a defect or a ground — that is the presumption of registrability in operation. Acceptance is not registration: section 33 accepts, publication and opposition follow, and registration comes later."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "accept the application"@en-AU,
        "accepted"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Both the Act and the Manual state it in terms, and the Manual explicitly ties it to the presumption of registrability."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Nothing specific."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0093" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(2)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "deferment of acceptance"@en-AU,
        "registration"@en-AU,
        "revocation of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/4%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0093 .

tmkc:GC-0094 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Available where information received after acceptance indicates the mark should not have been accepted. Distinct from revocation of registration under sections 84A to 84D, which the Manual gives a separate Part. GC-0042 already holds this term."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "revoke acceptance"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "revocation of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states it in one sentence. Written from Part 38 rather than from the section 43 material GC-0042 rests on; the overlap is flagged for a reviewer."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The overlap with the signed GC-0042."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0094" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s38> ;
    tmk:notLabel "acceptance"@en-AU,
        "rectification"@en-AU,
        "revocation of registration"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part38/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0094 .

tmkc:GC-0095 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual expects it to be rare and records that the Registrar is not obliged to consider it even on a third party's request. That discretion is the most examinable thing about the concept."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "revoke the registration"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "revocation of registration"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Stated in terms, with the discretion stated separately in the same passage."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part62/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Nothing specific."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0095" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s84A>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s84A(6)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "cancellation of registration"@en-AU,
        "removal for non-use"@en-AU,
        "revocation of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part62/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0095 .

tmkc:GC-0096 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's own gloss is the useful part: the acceptance period is 'set in abeyance'. That distinguishes it from an extension of time, which lengthens a period rather than suspending it."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "defer acceptance"@en-AU,
        "deferment"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "deferment of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual defines it in terms and contrasts it implicitly with the ordinary acceptance period."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether abeyance and extension really are different in effect, or only in procedure. The record asserts the first on the strength of one word."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0096" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s36>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s37(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.12> ;
    tmk:notLabel "acceptance"@en-AU,
        "extension of time"@en-AU,
        "lapsing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0096 .

tmkc:GC-0097 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Available across the Act wherever a time is set, and the Manual notes the procedure differs by which time is being extended. That variability is why it is one concept with many procedures rather than many concepts."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "extension of the period"@en-AU,
        "extensions of time"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "extension of time"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the general position at the head of its Part on the subject."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the legislative basis is right. `TMA1995/s224` is the general extension provision and the Manual's Part 15 covers several others."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0097" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s224>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r21.20A> ;
    tmk:notLabel "cooling-off period"@en-AU,
        "deferment of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part15/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0097 .

tmkc:GC-0098 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Automatic on the expiry of the acceptance period, so it is not a decision anybody makes. That is what separates it from rejection and from withdrawal."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "lapse"@en-AU,
        "lapses"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "lapsing of an application"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual quotes the statutory effect. Held because the vocabulary needs a way to say an application ended without anybody deciding anything."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Nothing specific."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0098" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s37> ;
    tmk:notLabel "rejection"@en-AU,
        "revocation of acceptance"@en-AU,
        "withdrawal"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part16/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0098 .

tmkc:GC-0099 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual defines it as a limitation of the exclusive rights given by registration, and explains that the owner never had exclusive rights in part of a mark anyway — so a disclaimer records something rather than creating it."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "disclaimers"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "disclaimer"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms by the Manual with the statutory reference attached."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part24/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether a disclaimer is a species of the section 6 'limitations' or a different instrument. The Manual's wording supports the first; the Act's structure the second."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0099" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s74>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s74(1)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "conditions or limitations"@en-AU,
        "endorsement"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part24/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0099 .

tmkc:GC-0100 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual treats an endorsement as what goes on the Register to record that an application was accepted on evidence or other circumstances. It is a record of how a ground was overcome, which makes it evidence about the mark's history."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "endorsements"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "endorsement"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states what an endorsement is for and when it is entered. Held apart from disclaimer because one records how a ground was overcome and the other limits a right."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the corpus defines 'endorsement' anywhere more directly. This record rests on a passage about when one is entered rather than on a definition."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0100" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(3)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "conditions or limitations"@en-AU,
        "disclaimer"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/6%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0100 .

tmkc:GC-0101 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Formal evidence filed to overcome a section 41 ground, once the Registrar remains satisfied after submissions that the mark is not capable of distinguishing. The Manual makes the sequence explicit and it matters: evidence comes after argument, not instead of it."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "evidence of use of the trade mark"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "evidence of use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the trigger, the sequence and the actor in one sentence. Held apart from 'use of a trade mark' because this is the proof, not the fact."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/3%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether evidence of use under section 41 and evidence of use under section 44(4) are the same concept. The Manual treats them in different Parts with different requirements."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0101" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(4)(b)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "evidence in support"@en-AU,
        "honest concurrent use"@en-AU,
        "prior use"@en-AU,
        "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part23/3%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0101 .

tmkc:GC-0102 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "A formal objection by a third party. The Manual notes that any person may oppose but that the opponent is generally somebody affected — which is a practice observation rather than a standing requirement, and the record keeps it in notes for that reason."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "opposition proceedings"@en-AU,
        "opposition to registration"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms at the head of the Manual's Part on the subject."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'any person may oppose' should be in the record rather than the notes. It is a statement about standing and belongs in a relationship record if anywhere."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0102" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s52>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2> ;
    tmk:notLabel "hearing"@en-AU,
        "rectification"@en-AU,
        "removal for non-use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0102 .

tmkc:GC-0103 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "A composite: the Regulations define it as a notice of intention to oppose plus a statement of grounds and particulars. Both components are separately defined terms, so the corpus holds three related definitions where a reader might expect one."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "notice of opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the composition in terms and cites both regulations. Held as one concept with the components named as near-misses, because the commonest error here is using the whole to mean a part."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the two components should be authored as concepts now. Both are defined terms in the candidate list with 44 and 47 Manual uses respectively."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0103" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.29>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2> ;
    tmk:notLabel "notice of intention to defend"@en-AU,
        "notice of intention to oppose"@en-AU,
        "statement of grounds and particulars"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part47/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0103 .

tmkc:GC-0104 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual grounds it in section 17: use is inherent in what a trade mark is, so a mark that is not used may be removed. The onus sits on the opponent once the application is opposed, which is unusual and worth carrying."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "non-use removal"@en-AU,
        "removal of a trade mark from the Register for non-use"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "removal for non-use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Stated in terms, with the section 17 rationale in the same passage — which is what ties this concept back to 'use of a trade mark' rather than leaving it as free-standing procedure."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part48/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the onus point should be a relationship record rather than a note."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0104" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s92> ;
    tmk:notLabel "cancellation of registration"@en-AU,
        "rectification of the Register"@en-AU,
        "revocation of registration"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part48/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0104 .

tmkc:GC-0105 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "A court remedy, not a Registrar's one: the amendment or cancellation results from an order of a prescribed court. That is what separates it from every other correction mechanism in the Act."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "rectification"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
