tmkc:GC-0127 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's Part 52 opens by listing what gets decided — oppositions to registration, to removal for non-use, to procedural matters — and section 205 makes a Deputy Registrar's decision the Registrar's."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "Registrar's decision"@en-AU,
        "written decision"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "decision"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The evidence is a list of what is decided rather than a definition of a decision, which is the weakest kind of support in this pass. The concept is held anyway because 178 Manual passages use the word and a knowledge base about examination that cannot say 'decision' is missing something structural."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "This record's evidence does not define a decision. Either Part 52 defines it somewhere this pass did not reach, or the record should be redrawn or dropped."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0127" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s205>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s35> ;
    tmk:notLabel "adverse report"@en-AU,
        "ground for rejection"@en-AU,
        "hearing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part52/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0127 .

tmkc:GC-0128 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 33(4) makes an opportunity to be heard a precondition of rejection, which is what ties hearings to examination rather than to opposition alone."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "ex parte hearing"@en-AU,
        "inter partes hearing"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "hearing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 33(4) states the entitlement in terms. The concept is drawn from the Act rather than from Part 51, because Part 51's opening is about how evidence is filed rather than about what a hearing is."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part51/1%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether ex parte and inter partes hearings are one concept. The Manual gives them different procedures."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0128" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s202>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(4)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "decision"@en-AU,
        "examination"@en-AU,
        "opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0128 .

tmkc:GC-0129 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "What the applicant claims, as against how it is classified and whether it is similar to something else. Amending it is one of the Manual's named ways of overcoming a section 44 ground. GC-0012 already holds this term."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "specification"@en-AU,
        "specification of goods and/or services"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "specification of goods and services"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The evidence states what a specification is for in the one place it does operative work in examination. That is thinner than a definition and is flagged. Overlaps the signed GC-0012."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/5%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Both the overlap with GC-0012 and the evidence, which is drawn from Part 27 rather than from the Part 10 section this record cites as its definition source."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0129" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s27(1)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.4> ;
    tmk:notLabel "classification of goods and services"@en-AU,
        "similarity of goods and services"@en-AU ;
